      "message": "Not yet — the coverage claim holds only for the dmi-integration suite, not all of CSIT.\nWhat\u0027s left in csit/ is actuator.robot with two tests:\nTest DMI Enhanced Healthcheck — GETs /actuator/health (the aggregate endpoint), asserts 200, body contains UP and, importantly, does not contain DOWN. K6 probes /actuator/health/liveness and /actuator/health/readiness instead. Those are the Kubernetes probe groups, not the aggregate — the Robot test\u0027s purpose, per its own documentation, is checking \"Database and diskspace status along with liveliness and readiness\". A DB or disk-space component going DOWN would fail the Robot test but not necessarily the K6 liveness/readiness checks. So that\u0027s a genuine gap.\n\nTest DMI Swagger UI — GETs index.html, expects 200. No K6 equivalent at all; nothing in the suite references swagger.",
